{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Flock.</b> For the obligation of the Paschal [offering]." "<b>And herd.</b> For shelamim [peace offerings]. And behold, the herd [cattle] are three thousand, after he said that all of them are for Paschal offerings on sheep and goats, and likewise they gave for Paschal offerings five thousand, and herd five hundred. And behold, the Paschal offering is mentioned before the herd, and likewise \"you and your house.\" And there are those who say that in Egypt he said \"sheep or goat,\" but now herd, if he is able. And the first is correct."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The passage references Numbers 28–29 sacrificial tallies (3,000 cattle, etc.); the syntax is compressed and several phrases are elliptical. 'וי״א' resolved as 'ויֵשׁ אוֹמְרִים' (and there are those who say)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:39.802936170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}